Reject intrabc dvs that start outside the tile or overlap the unreconstructed area.

The dv clipping in recon_b() is disabled (#if 0), so any decoded dv was used. A dv whose
source block overlaps the current block (e.g. a 16x8 block with dv (-15, 0) px) made the
bilinear copy memcpy() between overlapping rows (ASan memcpy-param-overlap in put_c,
mc_tmpl.c:56), and dvs into the not yet reconstructed area read uninitialized pixels. Add
the necessary conditions of AVM's av2_is_dv_valid(): the source must start inside the tile,
and it must not reach into the bottom-right quadrant from the block's top-left corner (local
and global intrabc ranges both exclude it, interpolation borders included). AVM fails the
frame with "Invalid intrabc dv"; return an error. Adds tests/test_intrabc_dv_validity.c.
Not fixed upstream as of 74bfb0ac.

Upstream: open MR videolan/dav2d!1017 (by rbultje, 2026-11-06; still open 2026-11-24) re-enables an intrabc dv validity check modelled on AVM's av2_dv_is_valid(); it is still marked TODO for CTC testing. Drop this patch once !1017 lands.

diff --git a/src/decode.c b/src/decode.c
index 86238056..5c6703f8 100644
--- a/src/decode.c
+++ b/src/decode.c
@@ -1107,6 +1107,22 @@ static int recon_b(Dav2dTaskContext *const t, DB_ONLY(const int depth)
         b->mv[0].x = (src_left - t->bx * 4) * 8;
         b->mv[0].y = (src_top  - t->by * 4) * 8;
 #endif
+        // AVM av2_is_dv_valid() / av2_is_dv_in_local_range(): the source block
+        // must start inside the current tile and must not reach into the
+        // bottom-right quadrant from the current block's top-left corner (the
+        // not yet reconstructed area, which includes the block itself); the
+        // reference decoder errors out with "Invalid intrabc dv" otherwise
+        {
+            const int r_border = !!(b->mv[0].x & 7) /* IBC_RIGHT_INTERP_BORDER */;
+            const int b_border = !!(b->mv[0].y & 7) /* IBC_BOTTOM_INTERP_BORDER */;
+            if (t->by * 4 * 8 + b->mv[0].y < ts->tiling.row_start * 4 * 8 ||
+                t->bx * 4 * 8 + b->mv[0].x < ts->tiling.col_start * 4 * 8 ||
+                ((b->mv[0].x >> 3) + bw4 * 4 + r_border > 0 &&
+                 (b->mv[0].y >> 3) + bh4 * 4 + b_border > 0))
+            {
+                return -1;
+            }
+        }
 
         DEBUG_BLOCK_printf("%*sfinal 2dmv: y=%d,x=%d\n",
                            depth, "", b->mv[0].y, b->mv[0].x);
